command-list: configure the commands tpm-rs does not implement as CC_NO

Classification: profile setting.

The implemented command set is a profile choice. Commands that tpm-rs does
not implement (tpm2-impl engine.rs SUPPORTED_COMMANDS) are configured CC_NO
so that both TPMs expose the same command set (TPM_CAP_COMMANDS,
TPM_PT_TOTAL_COMMANDS, TPM_PT_LIBRARY_COMMANDS) and reject the same command
codes with TPM_RC_COMMAND_CODE.

Commands configured CC_NO here: PP_Commands, PolicyCapability,
PolicyParameters, PolicyPhysicalPresence, SetAlgorithmSet, NV_DefineSpace2,
NV_ReadPublic2, ReadOnlyControl, PolicyTransportSPDM, VerifySequenceStart,
SignSequenceStart, VerifySequenceComplete, SignSequenceComplete,
VerifyDigestSignature, SignDigest, Encapsulate, Decapsulate, ECC_Decrypt,
ECC_Encrypt, EC_Ephemeral, ZGen_2Phase. Commands that tpm-rs implements but
the reference does not: none (so no harness exception is needed); the
TPM2_HMAC/TPM2_HMAC_Start and TPM2_MAC/TPM2_MAC_Start variants share their
command codes.

